From 1b87b8f33f60e5ee0d8f4c1473e562baa67578a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:21:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/35] Reconstruct 30 reference-only headers

Generate the headers present in the xnu-13432 DWARF source set but absent
from public xnu-12377.121.6: TCP segmentation/ECN/RBBR/timer, hypervisor
and PPL internals, enclave/exclave, telemetry, proc lifecycle, IOKit
address translator/analytics, and IOPM assertion types.

Declarations are derived from the KDK 27.0.1 DWARF type graph: struct and
union layouts with bitfields and arrays, enums with values, typedefs, and
function prototypes.  C++-specific member declarations that cannot be
expressed as free functions are recorded as comments.

Type relocations applied with the text of the public tree:
- struct tcp_seg_sent and its flag macros move from tcp_var.h to
  tcp_segment.h; tcp_var.h includes the new header.
- IOPMDriverAssertion{Type,ID,Level} and their kIOPM* constants move from
  RootDomain.h to IOPMAssertionTypes.h; RootDomain.h includes it.
- vm_map_store_types_internal.h is generated but its definitions still
  exist in vm_map_store_internal.h; relocation is a documented delta.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
